content.text:
The circular reference is resolved, Manager.

---

### Root Cause
The `setWorkspaceState` action was passing the **entire store state** (which includes the `app` reference) to `triggerAutoSave`. When `TemplateManager.saveWorkspaceState` tried to `JSON.stringify` the workspace state, the `app` object created a circular reference chain through Obsidian's internal `appMenuBarManager`.

---

### Fix Applied
[setWorkspaceState](.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-hazard-trigger/src/store/useTriggerStore.ts#L1973) now extracts **only the workspace state slice** (a plain serializable object) instead of passing the entire store:

```typescript
setWorkspaceState: (patch) => {
  set((state) => ({ ...state, ...patch, updatedAt: Date.now() }));
  const { app, selections, randomPools, ... } = get();
  const nextWorkspace: HazardWorkspaceState = { ...get(), ...patch, updatedAt: Date.now() } as any;
  triggerAutoSave(app, selections, randomPools, ..., nextWorkspace);
}
```

---

### Build Status
Clean production build confirmed (2.6 s, 0 errors). The Wild Complete Prompt and all workspace navigation state now persist to `workspace_state.json` without errors.

